From 4216b4707c5482fe953c625e1301315c96e5a2a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rmuxnet <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 12:48:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: retry Belize bridge enable attempts

Belize systems can still miss HDMI output on the first boot modeset even
when DPCD, AUX DDC, and EDID work. Manual TTY switches or display-manager
restarts can recover the display, which suggests that rerunning the
MN864729 bridge enable sequence and DP retrain during a later modeset can
fix the timing/order issue.

Run the MN864729 video bridge enable sequence and post-enable DP retrain
up to three times during bridge enable. The retry is bounded and only
happens in the bridge enable path, so it does not add background polling
or runtime overhead while the system is otherwise running.

The CUH-11xx path, bridge register values, EDID/DDC handling, mode
validation, and post-enable retrain mechanism are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: rmuxnet <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
